      connectBody: `<ol><li>Open the YM Bridge side panel, expand <strong>Tools</strong>, choose <strong>Settings</strong>, then open <strong>Extension settings</strong>.</li><li>In <strong>Last.fm setup</strong>, click <strong>Connect Last.fm</strong>.</li><li>Approve access on Last.fm. The extension stores the returned session key in Chrome extension storage.</li><li>Return to the panel and confirm that Last.fm is shown as <strong>connected</strong>.</li></ol>`,
      verifyTitle: "Verify delivery",
      verifyBody: `<p>Start a track in Yandex Music and open the side panel. The current title, artist and delivery target should appear. With normal network access, the target reads <strong>direct to Last.fm</strong>.</p><p>An empty queue can be normal while the current track is handled live. After an eligible listen is sent, <strong>Last delivery</strong> updates and the track appears in your Last.fm history.</p>`,
      alternativeTitle: "If the normal sign-in is unavailable",
      alternativeBody: `<p>Try <strong>Connect Last.fm</strong> first. If the direct authentication API cannot be reached, YM Bridge can complete the approved token exchange through its service.</p><p>The alternative username-or-email and password form runs only after you press its sign-in button. The credentials are sent once over HTTPS to obtain a Last.fm session key, the password is cleared from the form, and it is not stored by the extension or intentionally logged by the relay. See the <a href="/privacy-policy" data-locale-link>Privacy Policy</a> for the complete data flow.</p>`
